=== ISSUE ===
Title: update_study_chapter_tags can't set tags: it sends `name`, but the endpoint reads a `pgn` field

Per the Lichess API spec (https://github.com/lichess-org/api/blob/906d1a6e93ca1ba4b65c9decb3077f2431c6d55a/doc/specs/lichess-api.yaml), `POST /api/study/{studyId}/{chapterId}/tags` takes one form field, `pgn`: PGN text whose tag pairs are applied. An empty value deletes a tag, and omitted tags are kept. The tool's only input is `name`, sent as a form field the endpoint doesn't read.

=== PR ===
Title: fix: send study chapter tags as PGN text, as the endpoint expects
Body:
Closes #<issue>

`update_study_chapter_tags` now takes `tags: Record<string, string>` and posts `pgn` built as `[Name "value"]` lines, with PGN escaping for `\` and `"`. Tag names are validated as PGN symbols, and at least one tag is required.

Spec: https://github.com/lichess-org/api/blob/906d1a6e93ca1ba4b65c9decb3077f2431c6d55a/doc/specs/lichess-api.yaml

